{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779397226,"nonce":"EJAwGmVKhQgYwm0d1F8Ol2PCDd4=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDPrRWA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149#issuecomment-4512731480"},"message":"## Correction (post-deployment, 2026-05-21)\n\nThe Block 2 FCU param table in this issue lists four params to set today (`EK3_SRC1_POSZ` plus three `EK3_GPS_OFFS_X/Y/Z` rows). **The three `EK3_GPS_OFFS_*` rows are wrong** — those params don't exist on ArduPilot Rover for this firmware. MAVProxy returned `Unable to find parameter 'EK3_GPS_OFFS_X'` on Roland's first set attempt.\n\nThe GPS antenna lever-arm goes through `GPS_POS1_*` only, and that was already at the right values from PR #91 (`0.835 / 0.000 / -0.890`) — no change there was needed.\n\n**The only substantive FCU change today was `EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 3`.** That landed and bench-validated all three Phase 1 criteria. See the dev log entry \"Block 2 sanity check\" timestamped 2026-05-21T12:16 for the numbers.\n\nLeaving the brief unchanged in-place (post-deployment plans are historical record); this comment is the correction.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1779397808,"nonce":"45OYn0cr+N1O19fOwPby7bU9arw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDPvYiQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/149#issuecomment-4512798857"},"message":"## After-thought from wrap-up debrief (2026-05-21 EOD)\n\nTwo operator-driven ideas surfaced during the deployment debrief that field agents reading this via git-bug should be aware of:\n\n### Idea 1 — Platform-aware speed override + on-the-fly trackline editing\n\nTwo CAMP-side enhancements to give operators gentler intermediate options between \"let the trackline run\" and \"full manual override\":\n\n- **Speed override**: surface the platform's `default_speed` / `max_speed` (added to the platform message) as a CAMP slider for instant override.\n- **On-the-fly trackline editing**: drag a waypoint past an obstacle instead of taking the helm. Sidesteps the procedural trap that drove today's collision (manual override disengaged with boat *beside* not *past* the obstacle → cross-track-error correction back into the obstacle).\n\nAdded as a design thread to [`docs/roadmap.md`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/jazzy/docs/roadmap.md) under \"Class-ready operator UI\" → \"Design thread — defer past June 4\". Not promoted to issues yet — both pieces want scoping conversations.\n\n### Idea 2 — Camera tuning for OTH\n\nTwo focused issues filed:\n\n- [`#151`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/151) — **OAK keyframe interval tuning** for OTH lossy-path recovery. Measurement-driven; needs an OTH segment at a couple of settings.\n- [`#152`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/152) — **Rear camera over VPN** for backing-down ops and post-incident situational awareness on the Starlink path.\n\nCoordinated work — both touch the OAK encoder config and the boat→operator bridge topic budget; pick them up together.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1779460699,"nonce":"tEG+LmiZvfiUyxV2QIsJN7yQi+E=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABC7EYUM8AAAAGBSLedQ"},"status":2}]}